  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run (7 witnesses), so I used 1 of the 6 runs. No changes were needed after it.\n\n**Rule** (`LVMC_11_30_050.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a member of `DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian`.\n- **When it applies:** the pedestrian is on a roadway and not in a crosswalk. They are also on a carrier (a lane or the roadway itself) and moving across it within `p.crossing_motion_cos`. The lane case and the roadway case are written as two alternatives.\n- **The duty:** for every lane and every roadway the pedestrian is on and moving across, the motion must be at right angles within `p.right_angle_crossing_cos`. The obligation repeats that full selection of carriers, because the rule's two formulas can't share a region.\n- I added no narrowings of my own; the node's own reading of the \"right angles\" span covers it.\n\n**Witnesses** (`LVMC_11_30_050.lean` in `TrafficSpecWitness`): the road runs east–west and the pedestrian walks at 1.4 m/s. I used exact headings close to the planned angles:\n- **Diagonal crossing:** 36.9° off perpendicular instead of 40°; cosine 0.6, clearly between the two limits.\n- **Near-square crossing:** 5.5° off perpendicular instead of 5°; cosine about 0.095.\n\n| Scenario | Expected | Scene |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | violated | diagonal crossing of a one-way roadway with two lanes |\n| permit | compliant | near-square crossing of the same roadway |\n| idle | not applicable | pedestrian on the sidewalk |\n| blind | unknown | velocity masked |\n| branch_1 | not applicable | diagonal crossing inside a marked crosswalk |\n| branch_2 (added) | violated | roadway without lanes, so the roadway case decides |\n| branch_3 (added) | violated | two-way roadway with lanes and no roadway direction, so the lane case decides |\n\nI added branch_2 and branch_3 so that each of the two alternatives (lane and roadway) decides at least one test.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
